  m_text: These fires are particularly challenging because cooking oils and fats
    can reach extremely high temperatures, far exceeding their autoignition point,
    and they can splash and spread easily. Water is absolutely unsuitable here, as
    it can cause a violent explosive reaction known as "frothing" or "slop-over,"
    spreading the burning oil.
